Deferred from the 2026 modernization PR (#72), each worth a PR of its own:

- @emberx/test-helpers: setupOnerror(fn) and resetOnerror(), as in Ember, so a test can assert that a render
  or an action throws, instead of the error failing the test.
- @emberx/test-helpers: a test-waiter API (waitForPromise, buildWaiter, as @ember/test-waiters has), so
  settled() also waits for async work that is neither an @action nor a transition: a service's fetch, a timer.
  Then tests stop needing wait(500) or waitFor() to get past it.
- @emberx/component: @cached, which memoizes a getter until the tracked state it reads changes, and
  registerDestructor, for cleanup when a component goes away (the blog index route's setInterval, for one).
  Destructors only run on a renderer that destroys components: ember-source, PR #73, not @glimmer/core.

Can we currently pass environment variables to build? process.env.ENVIRONMENT (by default staging otherwise)

